# Wave W17-S (Route 127 Trench): kelp wall — forest-edge rock: a green-dark trench rock, deep sea-green in its body with brighter frond-green standing on its upper faces where the kelp forest crowds the wall\u2019s edge (design: kelp forest walling one side of the trench in swaying green — the wall kind carries the forest\u2019s colour, art layer only; the shipped kelpbed dressing itself stands byte-preserved). Route 127 Trench\u2019s own wall — the fleet\u2019s only green trench wall: split from Route 128 Trench\u2019s warm-seamed breathing rock by temperature (forest green vs cavern ember) and from Route 124 Trench\u2019s blue-grey shaft rock by hue entire.
